You are a senior enterprise product designer, behavioral UX specialist,
manufacturing-operations analyst, information architect, accessibility expert,
data-visualization designer and frontend engineer.

TASK

Redesign the existing Operationalyst application dashboard into a clear,
decision-oriented manufacturing intelligence product.

Do not redesign the public marketing homepage in this task.

Do not remove, delete, weaken or break any existing analytical functionality,
calculations, datasets, routes, imports, exports, reports, tools or modules.

The goal is to restructure and redesign the existing application so that:

1. Executives immediately see what requires attention.
2. Managers can understand why it is happening.
3. Analysts can inspect the supporting records and calculations.
4. Every major insight leads to a clear investigation or action.
5. The interface feels premium, controlled, explainable and trustworthy.
6. Existing P1-P5 analytical depth remains available.
7. First-time users are not overwhelmed by the entire system.

FIRST: INSPECT THE EXISTING PROJECT

Before changing files:

1. Identify the framework, routing structure and styling approach.
2. Identify all dashboard routes and sections.
3. Identify the current P1-P5 modules.
4. Identify shared components, charts, tables, forms and calculation logic.
5. Identify import, export, print and PDF functions.
6. Identify role-based or special views such as Executive, Dispatch Desk and
   Gate Kiosk.
7. Identify any demo data, customer names and generated metrics.
8. Document the existing functionality before modifying the interface.
9. Preserve all underlying calculations unless a genuine implementation error
   is discovered.
10. Do not replace real business logic with static mockups.

